    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present No. 78 Wingfield to the market. \n\nNestled just off the Enniskerry Road, minutes from Stepaside village and at the foothills of the Dublin mountains, this attractively presented three bedroom, two bathroom property boasts generous accommodation throughout including a separate home office/study, and is certain to be popular with the discerning purchaser.\n\nBuilt circa 2004, this excellent family residence boasts stunning views of the mountains from the front and of Dublin Bay from the rear. The property also benefits from a strong B2 BER rating.\n\nThree floors and approximately 125sq.m./1,347sq.ft. of well appointed living space comprises of an entrance hallway, living room with feature fireplace and doors leading to a well-proportioned, open plan kitchen/dining area with separate utility room and French doors leading to a picturesque rear garden.\n\nOnto the first floor and and you will find two bright and spacious double bedrooms, one to the rear and one with a front aspect benefitting from a feature balcony and box bay window. Concluding this floor is an excellent home office/study space with rear aspect and a tastefully designed family bathroom.\n\nAnother staircase leads to the second floor landing where you are greeted by an impressively large and light-filled master bedroom, with an arched window, velux skylight, fitted wardrobes and en-suite. To the other side of the landing is a convenient walk-in wardrobe and an additional storage space.\n\n To the rear of the property is a private, well-maintained garden with a patio and steps rising to a small lawn. A westerly aspect makes this an ideal space for outdoor dining and entertaining guests. To the front of the property there is ample space for parking.\n\nPositioned within 1km of Stepaside Village, no. 78 Wingfield Terrace is ideally located with an abundance of amenities on its doorstep such as Stepaside Golf Club, Leopardstown Village Centre, Woodruff Restaraunt and Quattro Woodfire Pizza. Carrickmines Retail Park is s short spin away as is Dundrum Town Centre. There are a number of choice schools within the area including Our Lady of the Wayside primary, Stepaside Educate Together and Rosemount secondary school to name a few. The Dublin Mountains are quite literally on your doorstep, further enhancing the list of leisurely activities available.\n\nOverall, this striking family home has plenty on offer for the discerning buyer and viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nGlass panelled hall door, semi solid wood flooring\n\nLiving Room - \nBright with semi solid wood flooring, feature fireplace and window overlooking green to front. Double doors leading to:\n\nKitchen Dining Room - \nWith semi solid wood flooring, window overlooking rear garden, wall and floor press units, electric oven and induction hob, stainless steel sink, double doors leading to garden\n\nBedroom 3 - \nRear aspect, fitted wardrobes and semi solid wood flooring, window overlooking rear garden\n\nStudy - \nRear aspect, semi solid wood flooring, window overlooking rear garden\n\nBedroom 2 - \nFront aspect, semi solid wood flooring, box bay window, balcony, wall to wall fitted wardrobes\n\nBathroom - \ntiled floor, full bath/shower suite with tiled wall side mirror, wc, whb, mirror\n\nMaster Bedroom - \nSecond floor, front aspect with view of mountains, semi solid wood flooring, fitted wardrobes, velux skylight, arched window, en-suite\n\nEn-Suite - \ntiled flooring, shower, skylight, wc, whb\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>B2 BER</li><li>c. 1,350sq.ft three-storey family home in excellent condition</li><li>Ideal location minutes from Stepaside Village</li><li>Gas Fired Central Heating</li><li>Built 2004</li><li>Master en-suite and walk-in dressing room</li><li>Private rear garden with patio and a sunny Westerly aspect</li><li>Stunning views over the Dublin Mountains</ul>"
      },
